==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{term|medeor||heal, cure|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈme.di.kus/|lang=la}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj-1&2|medicus|medica|medica|medicum|medicum}}

# [[healing]], [[curative]], [[medical]]
# [[Median]], Median language

====Inflection====
{{la-decl-1&2|medic}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|medicus|medici#Latin|medicī|m|second}}

# a [[doctor]], [[physician]], [[surgeon]]
#: ''Nuper erat medicus, nunc est vespillo Diaulus: <br> &nbsp;&nbsp;quod vespillo facit, fecerat et medicus.'' <br> (Lately was Diaulus a doctor, now he is an undertaker.  What the undertaker now does the doctor too did before.) &mdash; [[w:Martial|Martial]] I.xlvii (translation by Walter Ker).

